{"id":28108,"slug":"europe-51","title":"Europe ’51","year":1952,"country":"Italy","duration":109,"spine":674,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/28108-europe-51","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/322f040a60532b89f72da14f7ed9385f/5jeBrecMTVgwaM1S0SGmRxA1z8dEZ5_large.jpg","description":"Ingrid Bergman plays a wealthy, self-absorbed Rome socialite racked by guilt over the shocking death of her young son. As a way of dealing with her grief and finding meaning in her life, she decides to devote her time and money to the city’s poor and sick. Her newfound, single-minded activism leads to conflicts with her husband and questions about her sanity. The intense, often overlooked Europe ’51 was, according to Rossellini, a retelling of his own The Flowers of St. Francis from a female perspective. This unabashedly political but sensitively conducted investigation of modern sainthood was the director’s favorite of his films.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Roberto Rossellini","slug":"roberto-rossellini"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Ingrid Bergman","role":"Irene","slug":"ingrid-bergman"},{"actor":"Alexander Knox","role":"George","slug":"alexander-knox"},{"actor":"Ettore Giannini","role":"Andrea","slug":"ettore-giannini"},{"actor":"Giulietta Masina","role":"Passerotto","slug":"giulietta-masina"},{"actor":"Teresa Pellati","role":"Ines","slug":"teresa-pellati"},{"actor":"Marcella Rovena","role":"Mrs. Strada","slug":"marcella-rovena"},{"actor":"Alberto Plebani","role":"Mr. Strada","slug":"alberto-plebani"},{"actor":"Tina Perna","role":"Cesira","slug":"tina-perna"},{"actor":"Sandro Franchina","role":"Michel","slug":"sandro-franchina"},{"actor":"Maria Zanoli","role":"Mrs. Galli","slug":"maria-zanoli"},{"actor":"William Tubbs","role":"Professor Alessandrini","slug":"william-tubbs"},{"actor":"Alfred Browne","role":"Priest","slug":"alfred-browne"},{"actor":"Antonio Pietrangeli","role":"Psychiatrist","slug":"antonio-pietrangeli"}],"credits":[{"role":"Direc